<p class="note uwaga">The model assumes a wall facing due south and a rod perpendicular to it. The drawing does not reproduce the stucco decoration of the surviving dial — it shows the geometry of the three reckonings alone.</p>
<p class="note uwaga">The sun's position is computed for the leap year 2028, so 29 February can be chosen like any other date. The same calendar date does fall slightly differently against the solstices across the four-year cycle: near the equinoxes the sun's declination shifts by about 0.14 degrees either way, sunrise and sunset by under a minute, and the shadow by less than the width of a drawn line. The mechanical clock keeps that year's civil time, summer time included.</p>
